      "side": 1,
      "message": "ok, I added acquiring the lock before calling `flash_control_register_locked` and releasing it afterwards.\n\nbtw, I tried to acquire the lock twice:\n\n```\n\t/* Lock physical flash operations */\n\tcrec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(1);\n\tcrec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(1);\n\n\tret \u003d cros_flash_npcx_get_status_reg(dev, SPI_NOR_CMD_RDSR, \u0026reg);\n\n\t/* Unlock physical flash operations */\n\tcrec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(0);\n\tcrec_flash_lock_mapped_storage(0);\n```\n\nThe test still passes. I am 100% sure that `crec_flash_lock_mapped_storage` was called because I added a log and verified that `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` is enabled. Is my understanding correct:\n\n\"\"\"\nThe reason that the test does not freeze or deadlock despite multiple calls is that Zephyr\u0027s `K_MUTEX_DEFINE` creates a reentrant (recursive) mutex by default? Ia it true that in Zephyr `k_mutex` is designed to allow the owning thread to re-lock the same mutex multiple times without blocking?\n\"\"\"",
